 means all sorts of  you know wonderful things such as  blessing gift from heaven luck favor  intelligence etc it goes on and on and  on if it is a good thing megami probably  means it and you know what i'm just  gonna go ahead and say it this kanji is  opie and as such if you were a japanese  parent of any child then it would be  almost a crime not to assign them with  the megami kanji and as for fujiguru  this actually follows the gege akutami  protagonist naming scheme coming  directly from the fushigura plant in the  same way that yuji itatory takes his  name from the itadori plant sadly  however the kanji used to construct this  name pretty severely contrasts the whole  megami portion with fushi meaning to  drop or lower and guro simply meaning  black so i suppose the overall message  that we have with megumi fushiguru is  that he is a kind blessing lowered into  an extraordinarily dark situation which  definitely does seem pretty spot-on  considering his role in the series and  we can see this at work with fun factor  four which is that fushigura actually  becomes quite depressed when hishikigami  die as do i honestly because i was not  ready for the loss of divine dog model  white and i am legitimately terrified  every time fushigoro summons a shikigami  because every battle could be their last  but i'm also quite curious let me know  down in the comments below what your  favorite fushiguru shikigami is i'm  going to put in a preemptive vote for  max elephant because i do like the idea  of an elephant named max and this is  where fushigoro's kind-hearted niche  really shines through azakitami has also  identified him as the kind of person who  gets more upset when animals die than  when humans die which really highlights  the meaning of his name such a sweet boy  engulfed in horrific darkness  perpetually forced to use his animal  friends for combat it's sort of like  pokemon in a way just the more  high-stakes version and team rocket is a  cursed king who is trying to steal your  body because seriously nobody should  look at a 15 year old the way that  sukuna looks at fushiguru but maybe  sukuna is just curious because those who  have read both the manga and watch the  anime will note that fujikura's hair  differs quite greatly between the two in  the manga early fujiguru had quite  modestly spiky hair however the anime  turns his head into a full on hedgehog  and there's a couple of fascinating  reasons as for why this was done one of  which is that akutami is very conscious  that drawing fushiguru can often end up  looking like the frame of yuji so as  time went on akitami made fushigo's hair  longer and more hedgehog-like in order  to give him a stronger contrast to yuji  but this whole issue stems from  something even cooler than that because  when making the sequel jujutsukai-sen  series akutami had to create a new  protagonist being yuji but to keep him  distinct enough from yuta akutami gave  yuta's basic hairstyle to fushiguru  because i guess they really liked it and  didn't want to part with the style but  in addition to that yuji inherited  inumakiser so in a way the yuji and  fujiguru duo are just a flipped  perspective on the yuta and inumaki doer  and it's kind of crazy because now when  i look back at the chapters and i see  inumaki and yuta on the same page all i  see is yuji and fushiguru to bring  things back to something of a somber  note how six fun fact is not in fact fun  at all and that's because akitami has  confirmed that due to fujiguro's long  career as a judith sorcerer he has  actually had several friends die which  is interesting because in the series he  and kukisaki have a discussion about  death after that whole and that yuji  dying incident and fujigoro claims that  this is the first time that a classmate  of fierce has died being very specific  about the term classmate which i don't  know does that make our kitami's  statement even more depressing when i  first read that i thought it 