earching for this video i came  across a lot of fushiguro knowledge  dumps all of which mentioned his  birthday as something along the lines of  megami fushigo was born on december 22nd  and that makes him a capricorn which is  nice and all but for whatever reason  none of them seem to actually mention  the significance of the december 22nd  date this day falls smack bang in the  toji period for japan the winter  solstice essentially which occurs  between the 21st 23rd of december and of  course it is known for being the longest  night of the calendar year so that is  very significant because it further  emphasizes fushikura's relationship with  darkness if it wasn't bad enough that  his technique revolves around shadows  and the kanji for black is literally in  his name while he was also born on the  longest night of the year this man oh  boy i suppose cause he's not a man  whatever he is he is destined for  darkness furthermore toji also happens  to be the name of megami's father albeit  constructed with different kanji but the  intent is pretty clear it's a very  clever japanese pun and i love the  effort that akatami puts into small  details like this because think about it  megami was born ontoji from the peen of  toji for something a little less  profound fun fact number nine is all  about social interaction and in this  case specifically it has been noted by  akutami that fushigoro does not respect  his senpai inumaki by which i mean  fushiguru affords all of the superficial  respect that a child exactly one year  older than him deserves but the reason  why fushiguro has a secret bout of  disrespect is because inumaki gets  easily caught up in shenanigans quite  specifically the shenaniganory of panda  and gojo i suppose unamaki is a sort of  social chameleon who can adapt to  whoever is around him and sadly for  fushikura the concept of having not only  one but two gojos also known as gojai  for plural is quite a terrifying and  mildly annoying prospect but it is gojo  that leads us into fun fact number 10  which is that one day megami fujiguru  could very well be as powerful as satoru  gojo or potentially even greater  fushiguru is a great sleeping giant of  jujitsu kaisen someone who with each and  every arkhans up completely surpassing  every expectations i thought i had for  him and gojo himself has stated that  megami very much is the shining future  of this world and capable of at the very  least equaling him one day which is my  favorite fun fact of all because the  fushigoro hype train has well and truly  left the station at some points he even  feels more like the protagonist than  yuji does and in the end if fuji were to  die then i can see fushiguro being the  person who lingers and fulfills the gojo  role going forward in the next  generation and more on this topic here  is a bonus fact which is that gege  akutami has already decided how  fushigoro's story is going to end  whatever happens to this magnificent  hedgehog it is now set in stone which is  interesting because other characters  like yuji are admittedly still up in the  air and open for change so i'm not sure  whether to be happy or terrified that  fushigura has such a clear path forward  all i know is that i do trust gegekitami  to bring this character to a satisfying  conclusion no matter how happy or  depressing that may be for some enhanced  satisfaction however do go and check out  this video there is always more to learn  discover and enjoy about this series so  i look forward to seeing you there

